Wi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T21:32:49Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T21:34:24Z","body":"Ok, after closer look at the code, this is actually not that good xd\r\nI mean, the new plugins are identical to the WAV plugin. Literally 1:1 copy-paste.\r\n<img width=\"1820\" height=\"881\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/455d7cdb-4a80-4af9-b5a2-b81d2b4afb19\" />\r\nWhat's the point of adding this code just to soon remove it? If you want to _quickly_ add audio controls to MP3/OGG streams, with the intention to do it properly later, you can just modify `can_handle()` in `EditorInspectorPluginAudioStream` to return true for these types.\r\n\r\nHowever, since these editor are the same, you can make `can_handle()` pure virtual and then add EditorInspectorPluginAudioStreamWAV/MP3/OGG that only implement this method. That would achieve the same effect with much less code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5171967086/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5242887020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121882#iss